Consider the following two languages over the alphabet {𝑎, 𝑏, 𝑐}, where 𝑚 and 𝑛
are natural numbers.
𝐿1 = {𝑎𝑚𝑏𝑚𝑐𝑚+𝑛 | 𝑚, 𝑛≥1}
𝐿2 = {𝑎𝑚𝑏𝑛𝑐𝑚+𝑛 | 𝑚, 𝑛≥1}
Which ONE of the following statements is CORRECT?

#include <stdio.h>
int foo(int S[],int size){
if(size == 0) return 0;
if(size == 1) return 1;
if(S[0] ≠ S[1]) return 1+foo(S+1,size-1);
return foo(S+1,size-1);
}
int main(){
int A[]={0,1,2,2,2,0,0,1,1};
printf("%d",foo(A,9));
return 0;
}
The value printed by the given C program is _______ . (Answer in integer)

